{"ts": "2026-10-27T20:35:45.146393Z", "run_id": "r-20261027T2033Z-992f", "unit": "openspec:add-identity-model", "seq": 8, "type": "task.started", "task": "1.1", "title": "1.1 Write `src/identity/route.test.ts` first (imports from `./index.ts`; pure, no database: `IdentityError` has `name` `\"IdentityError\"`, its `code` and the given message and is an `Error`; the scenarios \"Known value and refused halves\", \"One organization\", \"None\" and \"Ambiguous\"; every rejection is checked with `assert.throws(fn, { name: \"IdentityError\", code, message })`), then implement `IdentityError` and `identityError(code)` in `src/identity/errors.ts` (`identityError` builds the error with the fixed message of design.md § Interfaces), `requireText(value, max)` in `src/identity/text.ts` (not a string, empty, longer than `max` UTF-16 code units, `!value.isWellFormed()`, containing `\"\\u0000\"` or `\"\\n\"`, or `value !== value.trim()` is `IDENTITY_INVALID`), and in `src/identity/route.ts` the real value of `IDP_ROUTE_KIND` (`\"idp\"`), `idpRouteKey` (`requireText(issuer, 2048)`, `requireText(organization, 255)`, then `issuer + \"\\n\" + organization`) and `organizationFromClaim` (an array of length 0 gives `IDENTITY_NO_ORGANIZATION`, of two or more `IDENTITY_AMBIGUOUS_ORGANIZATION`, of one is checked as the bare entry; a string is checked with `requireText(value, 255)`, any failure there, a non-string entry, and every other type including `undefined` and `null` give `IDENTITY_NO_ORGANIZATION`), all exported through `src/identity/index.ts` (types with `export type`), implementing requirements \"The IdP route key is exact\" and \"A token names exactly one organization\""}
